Climate Change (66.7%) says Climate change is a growing issue. El Nino Effects (33.3%) says El Nino affects weather patterns.

Flood Frequency argues that flooding is awful and happening too frequently now. Warm waters cause hurricanes that lead to flooding. People often ignore flood warnings until they are directly threatened. Flooding has severe consequences for homes and cars, but some people do not take responsibility. Local emergencies are being declared due to potential flooding from El Nino. Weather Warnings argues that Weather alerts have been issued.

@wrenkh.bsky.social: “Afternoon Kev I'm pleased you're ok. I do feel awful for those who're affected though. Flooding is awful & it's happening too frequently now.”

Flood Frequency (66.7%) says Flooding is happening too frequently. Weather Warnings (33.3%) says Weather alerts have been issued.

Green Politics argues that Green politics benefits everyone. Solar Expansion argues that We need more solar farms. The government should help homeowners install solar energy.

@linusd.bsky.social: “Green politics are for everyone, the young, the old, renters, immigrants, Palestinians, Jews, all of us. Thanks Mothin Ali for reminding us.”

Green Politics (55.6%) says Green politics benefits everyone. Solar Expansion (44.4%) says More solar energy is needed.

Electrification Benefits argues that Electrification is a good thing. Fossil Fuel Subsidies argues that Fossil fuels are expensive compared to clean energy. Fossil fuels are costly. Fossil fuel workers can transition to green infrastructure.

@justinmikulka.bsky.social: “Across the world, from India to Ireland, fossil fuels are heavily subsidized. And getting very expensive compared to clean energy. Good incentive for governments to accelerate the transition and end the costly subsidies.”

Electrification Benefits (57.1%) says Electrification is a good thing. Fossil Fuel Subsidies (42.9%) says Fossil fuels are heavily subsidized.

Diesel Export argues that stopping diesel export to US won't alleviate shortage. Canada should stop exporting diesel to US. Exported diesel is insufficient to solve US shortage. Fossil Fuel Subsidies argues that Governments subsidize fossil fuels.

@amias.net: “so not only will this cause widespread international fall out it will not actually help the diesel shortage. it might be enough to keep the us navy running but they are famously secretive about how much fuel they burn and the emissions they cause.”

Diesel Export (57.1%) says Stopping diesel export won't solve shortage. Fossil Fuel Subsidies (42.9%) says Governments subsidize fossil fuels.

Education.detail:
Public Schools Underfunded argues that Government reforms will exacerbate the crisis of underfunding public schools. Private schools are prioritized over public schools. Public schools are being closed and sold due to budget deficits. Private and charter schools shun special needs children. Voucher programs divert funds from public schools to private schools. School Choice argues that Private schools provide superior education. School choice relieves pressure on public schools. School Protests argues that Union leaders are supporting high school protests. Petitions are being signed to cancel high school pilots.

@prophetcassandra.bsky.social: “Disgraceful, private schools should have to pay much more than that”

Public Schools Underfunded (40.9%) says Public schools are underfunded. School Choice (36.4%) says School choice is beneficial. School Protests (22.7%) says Schools are being targeted to create a docile population.

Cornell Handling argues that Cornell punished accused men too leniently. The Cornell 7 were privileged and got away with their actions. Cornell Rape argues that a Cornell student was gang raped at a fraternity house. Many Cornell students claim they were sexually assaulted. A lawsuit was filed regarding a rape at Cornell.

@bluewriter25.bsky.social: “Cornell students stage sit-in to protest university's handling of alleged 2024 gang rape apnews.com/article/corn... I would like to read the essays written as punishment for hideous crime -wouldn’t you?”

Cornell Handling (88.5%) says Cornell mishandled sexual assault cases. Cornell Rape (11.5%) says Cornell student claims rape.

Higher Education Fails argues that Higher education has lost its way. University Management argues that University management is flawed.

@rogeramundson.bsky.social: “That's the way it's always been in higher education.”

Higher Education Fails (78.6%) says Higher education has lost its way. University Management (21.4%) says University management is flawed.

College Not Worth It argues that College is not worthwhile. Cosmetology Education argues that Community colleges should offer affordable cosmetology classes. Predatory private trade schools charge too much for cosmetology certificates. Cosmetology education should include small business curriculum.

@kalimurray.bsky.social: “What we should be talking about is supporting community colleges, and vocational high school to offer affordable cosmetology classes. The wait lists are insane. At least in the Black community, anyway, hairdressers and barbers play an important political role.”

College Not Worth It (60%) says College is not worthwhile. Cosmetology Education (40%) says Cosmetology education should be affordable.

Campus Crime argues that Universities violate the Clery act by not reporting crimes. Campus police may not be equipped to handle criminal cases. Sex Assault Response argues that Fraternities claim to go beyond legal requirements in disciplining perpetrators. Survivors can report trauma at any time and still deserve support.

@mcbridetd.bsky.social: “1200 sexual assault cases in 6 years. Only 7 expulsions or dismissals. Enough. 👇👇😡”

Campus Crime (57.1%) says Universities fail to report crimes. Sex Assault Response (42.9%) says Universities do not adequately respond to sexual assault cases.

School Support argues that Schools lack support for students. Job Market argues that the job market is bleak.

@clofsnitville.bsky.social: “...in the deaths of kids going to school. The other thing that I do see parents on here talking about and that I had experience with growing up is the impact on kids of having to get up deep in darkness and go to school before the sun rises. DO NOT RECOMMEND.”

School Support (66.7%) says Schools lack support for students. Job Market (33.3%) says the job market is bleak.

Student Loans argues that working conditions affect student learning conditions. Student loan policy seems mean and useless. Youth Work argues that Youth jobs are not beneficial.

@meganc.bsky.social: “There's this pervasive belief that a part-time job at a fast-food restaurant or ice cream shop or whatever is a good learning experience for teens but I had several of those jobs during high school/college and literally all I learned was that: 1. people suck 2. working sucks.”

Student Loans (66.7%) says Student loans have conflicting incentives. Youth Work (33.3%) says Youth jobs are not beneficial.

Other.detail:
Male Threat argues that Men pose a greater threat to women. Sexist Language argues that Men's language treats women as property. Language choice affects gender safety concerns. Sexist language perpetuates inferior species myth. Women Independence argues that Some women don't need a man in their life. Many women have been brainwashed by men to depend on them. Women's voices have been quieter due to societal expectations. Support Women argues that Men should listen to women. Men should stand with women and understand their perspective.

@jenzunleashed.bsky.social: “There could be equal amount of male and female victims? This is not a serious comment. Women literally live their entire lives being cautious of all men, being alone after dark, etc.”

Male Threat (46.7%) says Men pose a greater threat to women. Sexist Language (20%) says Language reflects women's status as property. Women Independence (20%) says Women can be independent without men. Support Women (13.3%) says Men should support women.

Child Abuse argues that He abused a child. Abuse Clarified argues that Abuse is clear, attraction is not.

@the2ndshootingstar.bsky.social: “its so hard to correct when ppl mix them up too 😭 "i think u meant to say predator. we know for a fact he abused children, but its not as clear if he was attracted to them or not" people MELT DOWN being told that kinda thing even when ur basically just reading them the dictionary”

Child Abuse (66.7%) says He abused a child. Abuse Clarified (33.3%) says Abuse is clear, attraction is not.

Car Free Areas argues that Cities should prioritize walkable spaces. Public Space Rules argues that off leash areas should be designated. camping outside hotels should be prohibited.

@velospence.bsky.social: “the thing people do want to go car free areas and that's why modern malls are designed like mini-cities with parking on the edges. once you're in, you hardly notice a car. they just lack the imagination to realize they'd be happier if their neighborhood was walkable.”

Car Free Areas (66.7%) says Cities should prioritize walkable spaces. Public Space Rules (33.3%) says Some public spaces have strict rules.
